```
Detection: Remote execution via PsExec-style tools (incl. renamed/clones)
MITRE ATT&CK: T1021.002 SMB/Windows Admin Shares, T1569.002 Service Execution
Data source: index=winlogs - System 7045, Security 5145, Sysmon 17/18

v2 - behaviour-based. v1 matched the service name PSEXESVC only and missed
every lateral-movement sample in EVTX-ATTACK-SAMPLES (renamed PsExec, RemCom,
cmd.exe services). Three signals, each tool-name independent:
  svc_install   7045 service whose command line is a shell/LOLBin, or a
                known remote-exec service name
  admin_exe     5145 an .exe written to ADMIN$ / C$ (tool binary staged)
  exec_pipe     Sysmon 17/18 pipe named <svc>-<host>-<pid>-stdin|stdout|stderr,
                the PsExec I/O pattern that survives renaming
Signals are correlated per host in 5-minute windows; more signals = higher
severity. Needs "Audit Detailed File Share" (5145) and Sysmon PipeEvent logging.
```

index=winlogs
    ((EventCode=7045)
     OR (EventCode=5145 (ShareName="*\\ADMIN$" OR ShareName="*\\C$") RelativeTargetName="*.exe")
     OR (source="*Sysmon*" (EventCode=17 OR EventCode=18) PipeName="*-std*"))
| eval signal=case(
    EventCode="7045" AND (match(ImagePath, "(?i)(cmd\.exe|%comspec%|powershell|rundll32|mshta|\\\\127\.0\.0\.1\\\\|\\\\admin\$)")
                          OR match(ServiceName, "(?i)^(psexesvc|remcomsvc|csexecsvc|paexec)")), "svc_install",
    EventCode="5145", "admin_exe",
    match(PipeName, "(?i)-\d+-(stdin|stdout|stderr)$"), "exec_pipe")
| where isnotnull(signal)
| bin _time span=5m
| stats dc(signal) as signal_count values(signal) as signals
        values(ServiceName) as services values(ImagePath) as image_paths
        values(RelativeTargetName) as files values(PipeName) as pipes values(src_ip) as src_ips
        by host, _time
| eval severity=case(signal_count>=2, "high", true(), "medium")
| sort - signal_count

```
False positives:
- IT staff using PsExec/PAExec for deployment (expect admin_exe + exec_pipe
  from known admin workstations; allow-list those src_ips after review)
- Installers that register services launching cmd.exe wrappers

Analyst triage:
1. Is src_ips a known admin workstation with a change ticket? Document, close.
2. Anything else, especially signal_count >= 2: treat as lateral movement,
   isolate the target host, and pivot to the source host.
3. On the source host, check Sysmon 1/10 just before this window for
   credential dumping that would explain how the attacker got admin rights.
```
